  "history": {
    "originCountries": ["Greece", "Cyprus"],
    "origins": "Pilotta is a Greek point-trick game of the Jass family, derived from Belote, and is particularly popular in Cyprus. It is played primarily in Cyprus, especially among younger players who often arrange pilotta meetings in cafés and cafeterias. The Greek counterpart played in Greece is named Vida. Ioannis K. Zapitis published rules in English and created the online version WebPilotta (gamesfair.com).",
